SOLUTION:

The optimal schedule meets both Karen and Mark with their minimum time requirements, considering the travel times and constraints. You start at North Beach at 9:00 AM. To meet Mark for 120 minutes within his availability (1:00 PM to 5:45 PM) at Embarcadero, the meeting is scheduled from 1:00 PM to 3:00 PM. This allows you to travel from North Beach to Embarcadero in 6 minutes, leaving at 12:54 PM to arrive by 1:00 PM. After meeting Mark, you travel from Embarcadero to Pacific Heights in 11 minutes, leaving at 3:00 PM and arriving at 3:11 PM. You then wait at Pacific Heights until Karen arrives at 6:45 PM. You meet Karen for the required 90 minutes from 6:45 PM to 8:15 PM, as her availability exactly matches this duration.

This schedule ensures both meetings are fulfilled with minimal idle time between activities, though idle time is not part of the itinerary output. The JSON below includes only the meeting actions.

{
  "itinerary": [
    {
      "action": "meet",
      "person": "Mark",
      "start_time": "1:00 PM",
      "end_time": "3:00 PM"
    },
    {
      "action": "meet",
      "person": "Karen",
      "start_time": "6:45 PM",
      "end_time": "8:15 PM"
    }
  ]
}
